{title: Lay you down}
{artist: Conway Twitty}
{key: G}
{comment: Structure: I V C V C V C}

{start_of_intro}
| G / / / |
{end_of_intro}

{start_of_verse}
[G]There's a lot of ways of sayin', what I want to say to you.
[D]There's songs and poems and promises and dreams that might come [C]true,
But I won't talk of starry skies or moonlight on the ground,
[D]I'll come right out and tell ya, I'd just love to lay you [C]down[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Lay you down and softly whisper pretty love words in your ear,
[D]Lay ya down and tell ya all the things a woman loves to [C]hear,[G]
I'll let you know how much it means just havin' you around,
[D]Oh Darlin' how I'd love to lay ya [G]down.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
[G]There's so many ways your sweet love's made this house into a home,
[D]You've got a way of doin' little things that turn me [C]on.[G]
Like standin' in the kitchen, in your faded cotton gown,
[D]With your hair all up in curlers, I'd still love to lay you [C]down[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Lay you down and softly whisper pretty love words in your ear,
[D]Lay ya down and tell ya all the things a woman loves to [C]hear,[G]
I'll let you know how much it means just havin' you around,
[D]Oh Darlin' how I'd love to lay ya [G]down.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse}
[G]When a whole lot of Decembers are showin' in your face,
[D]Your auburn hair has faded and silver takes it's [C]place,[G]
[G]You'll be just a lovely, and I'll still be around,
[D]And if I can I know that I'll still love to lay you [C]down[G]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Lay you down and softly whisper pretty love words in your ear,
[D]Lay ya down and tell ya all the things a woman loves to [C]hear,[G]
I'll let you know how much it means just havin' you around,
[D]Oh Darlin' how I'd love to lay ya [G]down.
{end_of_chorus}
